(1063554, 128410, 13749, '<td valign="top">interesting border/rotation.  i''m sure you''ll get a lot of comments on  how it may detract.  i don''t think it necessarily detracts or adds, but just looks a bit different.  anyway, not sure if that''s short DOF or motion blur - but you still have nice rendition throughout.  good work (i''m sure converting this to a normal border might have upped your score, although i don''t necessarily mind it)</td>', 'interesting border/rotation.  i''m sure you''ll get a lot of comments on  how it may detract.  i don''t think it necessarily detracts or adds, but just looks a bit different.  anyway, not sure if that''s short DOF or motion blur - but you still have nice rendition throughout.  good work (i''m sure converting this to a normal border might have upped your score, although i don''t necessarily mind it)', '2004-12-15 05:48:51.000000', NULL, 1),
(1063555, 128147, 29079, '<td valign="top">Very nice photo, like the colouring</td>', 'Very nice photo, like the colouring', '2004-12-15 05:49:49.000000', NULL, 1),
(1063557, 127985, 13749, '<td valign="top">great angle - interesting tear.  for the type of image that is normally conveyed here (ie: strong, bold, beautiful - especially considering the angle), a flag that wasn''t ripped might''ve been better.  obviously, that''s not so much in your control ;).  great job.</td>', 'great angle - interesting tear.  for the type of image that is normally conveyed here (ie: strong, bold, beautiful - especially considering the angle), a flag that wasn''t ripped might''ve been better.  obviously, that''s not so much in your control ;).  great job.', '2004-12-15 05:50:33.000000', NULL, 1),
(1063558, 128478, 13749, '<td valign="top">good, but i would''ve liked either slightly more or slightly less color in the foreground.  they''re not quite silhouettes, but not a lot of detail to look at either - leaves me unsure.</td>', 'good, but i would''ve liked either slightly more or slightly less color in the foreground.  they''re not quite silhouettes, but not a lot of detail to look at either - leaves me unsure.', '2004-12-15 05:52:56.000000', NULL, 1),
