(1073282, 128480, 25464, '<td valign="top">I knew this was yours.  It is absolutely wonderful, and WAY underrated.</td>', 'I knew this was yours.  It is absolutely wonderful, and WAY underrated.', '2004-12-22 02:03:56.000000', NULL, 0),
(1073335, 128444, 23458, '<td valign="top">Thanks for directing me here. You certainly have an interesting rationale for submitting your photo. I really like the point of view here, you have undoubtedly portrayed your reverence for the flag - additionally the stark contrast between the bright pole and the deep blue sky makes the image seem almost regal. As for the distracting lights, I see where you are coming from with them. If they do, in fact, serve to represent the two sides of the political equation, unfortunately I feel that the title loses something - the flag is clearly to the right, - this would indicate an almost unanimous political result, with little to no turbulence as you say. Now while the election result was relatively clear cut, there remains (From my outsiders perspective) great deal of idealogical division amongst the population...nitpicking I know, but I might as well be thorough. <br/> <br/>As for the aesthetics of the image, personally I feel that if you managed to clone out the lights you would be left with an extremely striking, minimalist image, that better conveyed your reverence and pride. Also, I would attempt to crop out some of the space at the top and side to make the angle of the pole appear more pronounced. <br/> <br/>Anyway, hope this has been somewhat constructive.<br/> <br/>Cheers<br/> <br/>Anders</td>', 'Thanks for directing me here. You certainly have an interesting rationale for submitting your photo. I really like the point of view here, you have undoubtedly portrayed your reverence for the flag - additionally the stark contrast between the bright pole and the deep blue sky makes the image seem almost regal. As for the distracting lights, I see where you are coming from with them. If they do, in fact, serve to represent the two sides of the political equation, unfortunately I feel that the title loses something - the flag is clearly to the right, - this would indicate an almost unanimous political result, with little to no turbulence as you say. Now while the election result was relatively clear cut, there remains (From my outsiders perspective) great deal of idealogical division amongst the population...nitpicking I know, but I might as well be thorough.  As for the aesthetics of the image, personally I feel that if you managed to clone out the lights you would be left with an extremely striking, minimalist image, that better conveyed your reverence and pride. Also, I would attempt to crop out some of the space at the top and side to make the angle of the pole appear more pronounced.  Anyway, hope this has been somewhat constructive. Cheers Anders', '2004-12-22 02:32:53.000000', NULL, 0),
(1073345, 127546, 25655, '<td valign="top">Wonderful photo. Congrats on your well deserved ribbon!<br/>I was dying to know how you did this, and I was amazed by the creativity shown.<br/>Great job!</td>', 'Wonderful photo. Congrats on your well deserved ribbon!I was dying to know how you did this, and I was amazed by the creativity shown.Great job!', '2004-12-22 02:45:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(1073346, 128337, 23251, '<td valign="top">Very nice shot Kirsty, best in the family...<br/> <br/>BTW your dad used your log in to leave you a message...  rotflmao.</td>', 'Very nice shot Kirsty, best in the family... BTW your dad used your log in to leave you a message...  rotflmao.', '2004-12-22 02:47:58.000000', NULL, 0),
(1073349, 128131, 1031, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Bran-O-Rama:</b></div><hr/><i> Crop is a bit tight. Seems like the spool is your focal point but I''d think you''d at least want the entire crank in the frame. The background and harsh shadow cast upon it does nothing for this photo. </i></td></tr></table> <br/>You win the prize for correctly identifying the largest number of weaknesses : )<br/> <br/>I have reasons/excuses for all of them which I won''t bore you with.<br/><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by zarniwoop:</b></div><hr/><i> Please don''t. Visual puns make me want to kill people. </i></td></tr></table> <br/>First a new camera, then a bigger hard drive ... maybe all of you who actually liked the "out of the box" thinking can chip in to buy me a Kevlar vest ...</td>', 'Originally posted by Bran-O-Rama: Crop is a bit tight. Seems like the spool is your focal point but I''d think you''d at least want the entire crank in the frame. The background and harsh shadow cast upon it does nothing for this photo.  You win the prize for correctly identifying the largest number of weaknesses : ) I have reasons/excuses for all of them which I won''t bore you with.Originally posted by zarniwoop: Please don''t. Visual puns make me want to kill people.  First a new camera, then a bigger hard drive ... maybe all of you who actually liked the "out of the box" thinking can chip in to buy me a Kevlar vest ...', '2004-12-22 02:49:30.000000', NULL, 0),
(1073364, 127510, 18349, '<td valign="top">I''m so happy for you Brandon!  Congrats! :o)</td>', 'I''m so happy for you Brandon!  Congrats! :o)', '2004-12-22 03:01:37.000000', NULL, 0),
