(1073368, 128131, 30980, '<td valign="top">I would have to state that the visual pun is one of the ONLY photos that didnt go for the obvious. You wouldnt believe how many photos there were of people blowing on things... is the topic breeze, or blowing, no its "wind". The word has many meanings, and to those who disparage at the pun, well.</td>', 'I would have to state that the visual pun is one of the ONLY photos that didnt go for the obvious. You wouldnt believe how many photos there were of people blowing on things... is the topic breeze, or blowing, no its "wind". The word has many meanings, and to those who disparage at the pun, well.', '2004-12-22 03:02:31.000000', NULL, 0),
(1073369, 128244, 18349, '<td valign="top">Congratulations on your blue!!!!!  :o)</td>', 'Congratulations on your blue!!!!!  :o)', '2004-12-22 03:02:48.000000', NULL, 0),
(1073373, 128131, 1031, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by damelzakelly:</b></div><hr/><i> I would have to state that the visual pun is one of the ONLY photos that didnt go for the obvious. You wouldnt believe how many photos there were of people blowing on things... is the topic breeze, or blowing, no its "wind". The word has many meanings, and to those who disparage at the pun, well. </i></td></tr></table> <br/>I think there were some clock photos working along the same (unsuccessful) line ... I knew where this would end up. But for me, the door was opened when the challenge description included NO examples, but only the adjective "ethereal"<br/> <br/>I didn''t have tome to organize and try my other variation on this idea ... hands blurred as they wind up a ball of knitting yarn.</td>', 'Originally posted by damelzakelly: I would have to state that the visual pun is one of the ONLY photos that didnt go for the obvious. You wouldnt believe how many photos there were of people blowing on things... is the topic breeze, or blowing, no its "wind". The word has many meanings, and to those who disparage at the pun, well.  I think there were some clock photos working along the same (unsuccessful) line ... I knew where this would end up. But for me, the door was opened when the challenge description included NO examples, but only the adjective "ethereal" I didn''t have tome to organize and try my other variation on this idea ... hands blurred as they wind up a ball of knitting yarn.', '2004-12-22 03:14:33.000000', NULL, 0),
(1073383, 127510, 14656, '<td valign="top">Thanks Laurie, I was long overdue! :D<br/> <br/>It also helped that I posted something other than a flag which voters were pretty tired of, myself included.<br/> <br/>Thank you all for your votes and the great comments. I''m puzzled how anyone could miss the wind in my photo? As for lack of a focal point, I really wanted to draw attention to the mist rather than the wave itself so I posted a shot with a really wild spray. I had many other pics with beautiful waves but the focus would be more on the water than the element of wind.<br/> <br/>All I was hoping for was a top 10 finish. Looks like Santa left me a yellow ribbon for the holidays!</td>', 'Thanks Laurie, I was long overdue! :D It also helped that I posted something other than a flag which voters were pretty tired of, myself included. Thank you all for your votes and the great comments. I''m puzzled how anyone could miss the wind in my photo? As for lack of a focal point, I really wanted to draw attention to the mist rather than the wave itself so I posted a shot with a really wild spray. I had many other pics with beautiful waves but the focus would be more on the water than the element of wind. All I was hoping for was a top 10 finish. Looks like Santa left me a yellow ribbon for the holidays!', '2004-12-22 03:23:50.000000', NULL, 0),
